SUMMARY:Newcomer Settlement Services
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261106T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261106T170000
UID:6a47defbe3c2e3fd937c22df@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:New to Canada? Need information on employment\, housing\, lang
 uage learning\, schools\, or other topics? A Settlement Worker can help. D
 rop in to meet our settlement worker every Friday from 9am - 5 pm.\nVisit 
 our branch or contact Ada Tao at 416-770-0312 or atao@cathcrosscultural.or
 g.\nIn partnership with Catholic Crosscultural Services.\nPlease bring you
 r immigration documents (PR card) with you
LOCATION:Burrows Hall
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a47defbe3c2e3fd937c22df
X-SOURCE:Volunteer Toronto
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Building Your Personal & Business Brand
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261118T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261118T160000
UID:6a9ae03ebe148200298c77e9@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This introductory workshop helps participants understand and m
 anage their personal brand in alignment with their professional goals. It
  covers key business branding elements and offers actionable steps to enh
 ance brand presence. Through interactive activities\, participants will a
 pply what they’ve learned to develop both personal and business brands\
 , while exploring marketing strategies and campaign elements.\nInformatio
 n Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected b
 y the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(
 a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and pr
 ogram registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the libr
 ary handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswe
 rline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Maria A. Shchuka\, 1st floor the Children's Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a9ae03ebe148200298c77e9
X-SOURCE:Volunteer Toronto
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Access to Housing
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260923T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260923T160000
UID:6a3c343bc7d3cd580062952b@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Are you seeking housing support or have questions about afford
 able housing options? Join us at S. Walter Stewart Library for personalize
 d\, one-on-one assistance with a Housing Services Worker.\nEast York Housi
 ng Help Hub is offering information session on the Rent Geared to Income o
 ptions available in\nMyAccesstoHousingTO\nonline system. Housing staff wil
 l support program participants with hands-on supports and help them comple
 te the registration process.\nFor more information or to register please c
 ontact East York Housing Help Hub at 416 698-9306 or email eyhhc@eyetfrp
 .ca.
LOCATION:S. Walter Stewart
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a3c343bc7d3cd580062952b
X-SOURCE:Volunteer Toronto
END:VEVENT
